All 15 tests pass. Here's what I fixed across `src/`:

**`src/auth.py`**
- `has_permission`: lowercased both sides so role matching is case-insensitive.
- `is_admin_or_owner`: changed `and` to `or` — being either an admin or the owner should grant access.

**`src/inventory.py`**
- `__init__`: replaced the mutable default `{}` with `None` plus `dict(initial)` to prevent instances from sharing state.
- `add`: changed `self._stock[sku] = qty` to `+=` accumulation so repeated adds increase stock.
- `reserve`: relaxed `qty >= available` to `qty > available`, allowing reserving exactly the full available amount.
- `release`: added a guard so releasing more than the currently reserved amount raises `ValueError`.

**`src/text_utils.py`**
- `slugify`: applied `.lower()` to the input and added a `while "--" in collapsed:` loop to fully collapse repeated separators.
- `truncate`: subtracted `len(suffix)` from the slice length so the total output respects `max_len`.
